### Golang: Basic Google Search Integration\
\
Source: https://serpapi.com/integrations/go\
\
This example demonstrates how to perform a basic Google search using the SerpApi Go client. Ensure your SERPAPI_KEY is set as an environment variable. It searches for 'Coffee' in 'Austin, Texas, United States'.\
\
```go\
package main\
\
import (\
  "github.com/serpapi/serpapi-golang"\
  "os"\
  "fmt"\
  "log"\
)\
\
func main()\{\
  // replace with your SerpApi key\
  setting := serpapi.NewSerpApiClientSetting(os.Getenv("SERPAPI_KEY"))\
  setting.Engine = "google"\
  // initialize the client\
  client := serpapi.NewClient(setting)\
  parameter := map[string]string\{\
    "q": "Coffee",\
    "location": "Austin, Texas, United States",\
    "hl": "en",\
    "gl": "us",\
    "google_domain": "google.com",\
  \}\
  results, err := client.Search(parameter)\
  if err != nil \{\
    log.Fatal(err)\
  \}\
  fmt.Println(results)\
\}\
```\
