### GET /search.json - Retrieve Forums Data\
\
Source: https://serpapi.com/tripadvisor-search-api\
\
This endpoint allows you to search for data, including forum discussions, using specified engines and parameters. The example shows how to retrieve forum data from TripAdvisor.\
\
```APIDOC\
## GET /search.json\
\
### Description\
Retrieves search results from various engines, including forum data when applicable. This example focuses on using the TripAdvisor engine to find Rome-related forums.\
\
### Method\
GET\
\
### Endpoint\
https://serpapi.com/search.json\
\
### Query Parameters\
- **engine** (string) - Required - The search engine to use (e.g., `tripadvisor`).\
- **q** (string) - Required - The search query (e.g., `Rome`).\
- **ssrc** (string) - Optional - Source parameter, used here to specify forums (`f`).\
- **api_key** (string) - Required - Your SerpApi key.\
\
### Request Example\
```\
https://serpapi.com/search.json?engine=tripadvisor&q=Rome&ssrc=f&api_key=YOUR_API_KEY\
```\
\
### Response\
#### Success Response (200)\
- **forums** (array) - A list of forum discussion objects.\
  - **position** (integer) - The position of the forum in the results.\
  - **title** (string) - The title of the forum thread.\
  - **forum_id** (integer) - The unique identifier for the forum.\
  - **link** (string) - The URL to the forum thread.\
  - **location** (string) - The location associated with the forum.\
  - **date** (string) - The date of the forum post.\
  - **user** (object) - Information about the user who posted.\
    - **username** (string) - The username of the poster.\
    - **link** (string) - The URL to the user's profile.\
    - **avatar** (string) - The URL to the user's avatar.\
  - **highlighted_comment** (object) - The highlighted comment from the forum post.\
    - **text** (string) - The full text of the highlighted comment.\
    - **highlighted_texts** (array) - An array of strings that were highlighted.\
- **serpapi_pagination** (object) - Pagination information for the results.\
  - **next** (string) - URL for the next page of results.\
\
#### Response Example\
